# Wing Night environment. Copy to .env only if you need to override a default —
# a normal checkout needs nothing in here.

# Where the night's real content lives: roster, teams, party music, generated
# heads, GEO photos. Defaults to ~/wing-night-content when that directory
# exists, and to this repo's own content/ when it does not, so a fresh clone or
# worktree boots either way with no setup. Set this only to point a run at a
# different pack (a second party, a throwaway copy).
#
# The directory holds the `local/` layer of a content root:
#   <pack>/.env                       GEMINI_API_KEY for `pnpm import:avatars`
#   <pack>/local/players.json         roster (avatarSrc is pack-relative)
#   <pack>/local/teams.json           teams, genres, anthem filenames
#   <pack>/local/audio/lobby/*.mp3    SETUP lobby playlist
#   <pack>/local/teams/audio/*.mp3    team anthems
#   <pack>/local/assets/avatars/*     generated heads, served by the server
#   <pack>/local/assets/geo/*         GEO photos, served by the server
#   <pack>/local/avatar-sources/*     input photos + manifest for import:avatars
#
# Anything the pack does not carry (gameConfig.json, the minigame prompt banks)
# falls back to this repo's committed content/sample/.
# WN_CONTENT_ROOT_DIR=/Users/you/wing-night-content

# Host control token for the tablet. Unset means LAN-open, which is the party
# default.
# HOST_CONTROL_TOKEN=

# Server port. The client resolves the server at :3000 by default.
# PORT=3000
